CM ============================================================
CM  TM-SC-NEC-004: Screwdriver Antenna — 17m Band
CM  2.4m whip, base loading coil, 4 horizontal elevated radials
CM  Frequency: 18.068–18.168 MHz (5 points, 0.025 MHz step)
CM
CM  Loading coil (series RL at base, segment 1 of GW1):
CM    R = 0.739 ohm  (Rcoil = Xant / Q, Q~340)
CM    X = 251.1 ohm  (XL required to resonate 2.4m whip on 17m)
CM
CM  Whip: 2.4m, avg radius 0.006m, 20 segments
CM  Radials: 4 x 2.4m at z=0.005m, 90 deg spacing
CM  Ground: real (Sommerfeld-Norton), eps=13, sigma=0.005
CM  Feed: 1V voltage source at GW1, seg 1
CM
CM  Tuning note: 17m is WARC-only, 100 kHz wide. SWR bandwidth
CM  of a loaded whip is narrow — expect 2:1 BW of ~50 kHz or less.
CM  Screwdriver tuning precision is essential for CW vs SSB segments.
CM  18.068 MHz lower edge; 18.168 MHz upper edge.
CM ============================================================
CE
